      "body": "## Original biology course and offline cross explorer — 68094585a1c2 / memory_delivery\n\nUnder Jacob's standing HAMON execution mandate, add a learner-facing Mendelian-inheritance lesson and a small offline gamete-to-offspring explorer. This extends RecallWeave's cellular-energy and enzyme material with an original introductory biology course that learners can import, study, review, practice and keep as notes.\n\n### Current source and ownership\n\nFresh source is main `3cdebd86e69506709bcaeaeff4026deb3d1fc208`, complete tree `4d8cfac84b84818af1a7e13cfa4d569fdbbef2d6` (871 leaves; no AGENTS.md, CONTINUE.md, CONTRIBUTING or CODEOWNERS). All 59 current project issues/PRs, including closed records, the refreshed 24 open scopes, and 386 central HAMON #140 comments through6062059500 were checked. No Mendelian-inheritance, gamete-cross or genetics teaching owner/path was found. This is an external source scope, not a native lease.\n\nExisting importer, learner/model, authoring, unfinished/completed archives, focused lessons, catalog, handout, and every separately owned course/explorer remain with their owners. In particular #44, #49, #50 and the Boolean/Markov/sorting/feedback/trace-comparison scopes are preserved.\n\n### Learner result\n\n- Twelve original questions with worked explanations, misconception reasoning and transfer prompts about paired alleles, equal segregation, genotype versus phenotype, one-locus crosses and explicitly independent two-locus crosses.\n- A direct-open lab lets a learner choose bounded parental genotypes, inspect their gametes, follow each fertilization cell, and compare exact genotype and phenotype fractions.\n- The lab uses hypothetical plant crosses, diploid autosomal loci, equal segregation, random fertilization and explicitly stated complete dominance/independent assortment. It presents probabilities, not a guarantee of a particular finite offspring count.\n- Explicit downloads save the checked original course JSON and the current computed cross. Existing local-file preview/start, review/practice and study-note flows receive the course.\n\n### Additive source fence\n\nNew paths only:\n- `courses/mendelian-inheritance.json`, `courses/mendelian-inheritance.md`, `courses/mendelian-inheritance-lab.html`\n- `templates/mendelian-inheritance-lab.html`\n- `src/mendelian-inheritance.mjs`, `src/mendelian-inheritance-ui.mjs`\n- `tools/build-mendelian-inheritance.mjs`, `tools/check-mendelian-inheritance-browser.mjs`\n- `tests/mendelian-inheritance.test.mjs`, `tests/mendelian-inheritance-course.test.mjs`\n- Unique receiving evidence under `docs/receiving/mendelian-inheritance-68094585a1c2/`\n\nA small README discovery entry may be composed over its then-current content after qualification. No catalog manifest, shared learner/importer/validator/model, existing course, dependency or workflow edit belongs to this scope.\n\n### Content and native receiving\n\nScientific background is checked against OpenStax *Biology 2e* [12.2](https://openstax.org/books/biology-2e/pages/12-2-characteristics-and-traits) and [12.3](https://openstax.org/books/biology-2e/pages/12-3-laws-of-inheritance), with NHGRI definitions where useful. Questions, scenarios, wording and diagrams are original; source exercises, passages and figures are not copied.\n\nIndependent content receiving will solve the frozen questions and calculations before comparison with the authored key. Native checks use the current deck parser and learning/review contracts, with independent cross arithmetic and exact saved-file checks. Actual installed-browser receiving covers both the lab and the current modular/standalone learner, including explicit import, completion, separate practice, notes download, keyboard use and a narrow viewport. No measured learning-efficacy claim or runtime provider call is intended.",
